-- title:
--   Étale-local existence of Schrödinger frames of type δ
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $g,d,n$ and a tuple $\delta : \mathrm{Fin}\,g \to \mathbb{N}$ with all $\delta_i$ nonzero and $\prod_i \delta_i = d$, and a commutative ring $S$ in which the image of $d$ is a unit. Let $u$ be a polarised abelian scheme of invariants $(g,d,n)$ over $S$: a scheme $A$ with structure morphism $u.f : A \to \operatorname{Spec} S$, a commutative relative group law $u.L$ (functorial group structures on the sets of $S$-morphisms into $A$ over a varying base, natural in the base), the bundle of abelian-scheme properties, fibres of topological Krull dimension $g$, sections $P_0,\dots,P_{2g-1}$ killed by $n$ which in every geometric fibre over an algebraically closed field are independent and span the $n$-torsion, and an invertible module $u.\mathrm{pol}$ on $A$ whose sections give a closed immersion into projective space and whose geometric fibres have $H^0$ of dimension $d$. Assume $u$ is rooted symmetric of type $\delta$, i.e. $u.\mathrm{pol}$ is locally isomorphic over the base to its pullback by inversion, $u$ satisfies `IsOfType δ` (étale-locally the kernel of the polarisation is generated by a geometrically injective homomorphic family of sections indexed by the group attached to $\delta$), and $u$ satisfies `HasPrincipalRoot` (flat-locally $u.\mathrm{pol}$ is a tensor product of powers of an invertible module with trivial kernel and of its inversion pullback). Then there exists a commutative ring $S'$, an $S$-algebra structure on $S'$ that is faithfully flat and étale, together with a Schrödinger frame for $u.f$, $u.L$, $u.\mathrm{pol}$ along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $S \to S'$ and of type $\delta$: global sections $\sigma_h$ of the pullback of $u.\mathrm{pol}$ to $A \times_S \operatorname{Spec} S'$, indexed by $H(\delta) = \prod_i \mathbb{Z}/\delta_i$, such that $c \mapsto \sum_h c_h \sigma_h$ is a bijection from $S'^{H(\delta)}$ onto those sections, together with theta points $\mathrm{lift}(h)$ for $h \in H(\delta)$ and $\mathrm{dualLift}(\chi)$ for additive characters $\chi$ of $H(\delta)$ valued in $S'$, acting by $\mathrm{lift}(h)\cdot\sigma_{h'} = \sigma_{h+h'}$ and $\mathrm{dualLift}(\chi)\cdot\sigma_h = \chi(h)\,\sigma_h$.
--
--   This is the étale-local normalisation of the theta group action on the sections of a symmetric, principally rooted polarisation of separable type $\delta$: after a faithfully flat étale base change, the global sections acquire a Schrödinger basis on which the Heisenberg-type operators act by translation and by characters. It is used in the construction of theta structures, via [`AlgebraicGeometry.PolarisedAbelianScheme.thetaTypeLocally_of_rootedSymmetricOfType`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.PolarisedAbelianScheme.thetaTypeLocally_of_rootedSymmetricOfType).
